# RoboArena delivery workflow

Aligned with global `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`. Where this rule and that file agree, follow both. Repo-only extras (identity, ledger, engineering) are below.

## Git & branching

- **No AI attribution.** Never add `Co-Authored-By: Claude` (or any AI co-author). Omit it entirely — no substitute line.
- **Check the current branch first.** Before any branch decision, read the current branch — the user may already be on the branch they want. If so, use it.
- **Branch per task/phase, not per component; never build on the default branch.** One branch covers a whole task or phase, spanning however many components it touches. Reuse before creating: check current branch and existing task branches first. For parallel/independent tasks, cut multiple branches from origin at the same time, one per task — develop each in isolation, then PR/commit/push back to the parent branch only once all of them are done. When unsure whether something is its own task/phase or part of the current one, ask.
- **Naming (when creating a branch):** `feat/task-<N>-<slug>` (or `feat/<phase>-<slug>`). Base: current `master` tip, or a parent task branch tip when stacked on unfinished sibling work.
- **Small work doesn't get a branch.** One-liners, typos, tweaks, fixes scoped to a file or two → commit on the current branch. Exception: if the current branch is the default branch (`master` / `main`), still branch first.
- **Never commit product work on `master`.**
- **Commit by logical chunk, not per-component.** Group related changes that belong together into one commit, even across files — don't mechanically split every component (or every RED/GREEN step) into its own commit. Only split when changes are genuinely independent. Each commit should stand alone with a clear message. Not one end-of-task dump.
- **Push once per task/phase by default** — commit as you go; one push when the task/phase is done. Push mid-work only when needed (user asks, or teammates need the remote). Don't leave a finished task unpushed.
- **PR/merge to master is never automatic.** Never open a PR or merge to `master` without explicit confirmation — always ask first.

## Parallel tasks and landing

- Parallel **coding** on disjoint files / worktrees is fine.
- For a plan wave with multiple independent tasks: develop each on its own branch; only after they are done, ask whether to PR/merge — and then land **one branch at a time** in dependency order (no parallel merges).
- Do not merge mid-wave just to unblock unless the user asks.

